# "When you discard a nonland card this way": discarding a land does not trigger the reflexive ability, and neither does
# declining the discard ("you may"). Bot1 casts Glacial Dragonhunt twice (turn 3 and turn 5, off two Moxen): on turn 3 it
# discards an Island (a land card), on turn 5 it discards nothing. Bot2's Concealing Curtains is never damaged, the
# Dragonhunt draws a card each time, and with a creature to target the refusal is not for lack of one.
# The positive control (the nonland discard) is glacial-dragonhunt-discarding-a-nonland-card-deals-three-damage-...

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Glacial Dragonhunt
Glacial Dragonhunt
Island x3
Island
Island
Island
Plains
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Concealing Curtains
Plains x14

